<map>
	<name> CMP Tarawa </name>
	<briefing locid="The Battle of Tarawa primarily took place on Betio Island in the Tarawa Atoll of the Gilbert Islands chain.  The forces of the 2nd Marine Division were tasked with landing and securing Betio, opposed by the 7th Sasebo Special Naval Landing Force (SNLF).  It was boasted by its defenders that a million Americans couldn't take Tarawa in 100 years.  On 20 November, 1943 - As the battle started, the 2nd Marines quickly realized they had overestimated the depth of the reef surrounding the island, and many in LCVP's were forced to exit and wade ashore more than 500 yards under heavy fire with no cover.  After 3 days of fighting the island was secured, the US learning in the process that amphibious landings in the Pacific would come at a heavy price.  Map made by Pr0z4c.  Special thanks to the CMP Mapping Team.">map description for modders maps not localized (english only)</briefing>
	<music> Levels/cmp_tarawa/sound/Tarawa.ogg</music>
<modes>
